    "Exact normalized matching groups on content_hash digest alone; it does not byte-confirm normalized content equality in exact_duplicates.",
    "MinHash candidate pairs are verified using MinHash estimate, not exact Jaccard, per implementation.",
    "Union-find clusters can include pairs below configured threshold; verified edge list is preserved separately.",
    "Module header reverses false-positive/negative labels in explanatory parentheticals; implementation/formula govern behavior.",
    "Word tokenizer accepts ASCII letters and digits only: distinct Cyrillic-only and CJK-only strings become empty token sets and cluster with Jaccard 1.0 in the recorded public API controls. This English-oriented text method must not establish file equality.",
    "content_only removes negation tokens: inserting not alone in the recorded sentence produces Jaccard 1.0; changed bind/binds control remains distinct.",
    "Default content_hash is 16 hexadecimal digits (64 bits); make_id defaults to 12 hexadecimal digits (48 bits). Digest equality alone is not a proof of equal file bytes.",
    "NoveltyGuard TF-IDF constructs a pair-fitted vectorizer without passing configured min_document_frequency. DuplicateFinder passes it; at values 2 and 3, alpha/beta become zero vectors and cluster at cosine 1.0, while guard reports similarity 0.0 and novel.",
    "Original LSH test named candidates_are_a_superset_of_the_verified_duplicates only checks that returned candidates have positive MinHash similarity; it does not establish exhaustive recall of true duplicates.",
